<interrogationes unitas="provenientia">

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I make a new house binary answer -provenientia?
    <responsum symbolum="provenientia_respondere ProvenientiaRelatio" via="tools/stml.c tools/provenientia_scribere.sh">Declare
      the generated record and link its object through an aedilis
      annotation, as tools/stml.c does: a comment
      &lt;aedilis obiectum="build/fabrica/provenientia/T.c"/&gt;,
      externus constans ProvenientiaRelatio provenientia_T; and as the
      FIRST statement of principale: si
      (provenientia_respondere(argc, argv, &amp;provenientia_T)) redde
      ZEPHYRUM. The installer runs tools/provenientia_scribere.sh T ARTIFICIUM
      before building, which writes that .c file.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quid">
    <quaestio! (>what does the -provenientia report contain and who reads it?
    <responsum symbolum="provenientia_textus provenientia_respondere" via="tools/fabrica_sutura.c">Four
      lines: 'provenientia 1', 'artificium X' (e.g. bin/manus),
      'ingressus H' (the fabrica digest of the inputs of the action
      that built it) and 'commissum C' (short HEAD hash, with
      ' SORDIDUM' when the tree had uncommitted changes). bin/fabrica
      runs the installed binary with -provenientia and compares the
      digest with the one it computes today: equal means the install is
      fresh. A non-zero exit or empty output counts as no
      report.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="cur">
    <quaestio! (>why is the record passed as an argument instead of the library linking a well-known symbol?
    <responsum symbolum="provenientia_respondere ProvenientiaRelatio" via="include/provenientia.h">Four
      installers link build/ objects blindly. If lib/provenientia.c
      referred to a symbol that only the generated file defines, every
      binary that links the library without that file would fail to
      link (fabrica plan 1a T7). So the binary names its own generated
      record and hands it in.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="cur">
    <quaestio! (>why must provenientia_respondere be called before anything else in principale?
    <responsum symbolum="provenientia_respondere" via="tools/fabrica_fumus.sh">bin/fabrica
      asks from whatever directory it is in, so the answer must not
      depend on the working directory, configuration or any other
      setup the tool does. It matches only when -provenientia is the
      ONE argument (argc == II); it then writes the report to stdout
      and returns VERUM, and the caller exits 0. In every other case it
      writes nothing and returns FALSUM. The smoke test checks it from
      a foreign directory.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="possumne">
    <quaestio! (>can the ingressus field be something other than a 64-character hex digest?
    <responsum symbolum="ProvenientiaRelatio" via="tools/provenientia_scribere.sh">Yes,
      despite the header's 'LXIV hex': the generator writes 'ignotum'
      when bin/fabrica is not built yet (bootstrap), or when 'bin/fabrica
      digestum' fails and PROVENIENTIA_TOLERANS=1 is set (without that
      variable a failing digest stops the generator with exit 1).
      commissum is 'ignotum' outside a git tree. A reader of the report
      should treat any value that is not 64 hex digits as unknown,
      never as fresh.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

</interrogationes>
